the Trump administration is moving  hundreds of migrant children from a  Clint Texas Border Patrol facility where  they were held in conditions described  as squalid and unsanitary now we first  reported on those conditions there last  week Omar Villafranca is in Mission  Mission Texas where migrant families  often cross the border there Omar the  details of the story are so upsetting  and I guess the question now is where  are the kids  well good morning a spokesperson with  the office of refugee resettlement told  us that the majority of those children  in the Clint facility will now be moved  over into their care where we're not  exactly sure as for the 50 or so  children who were not being transferred  we don't know what's going to happen to  them now this all comes as attorneys  recently toured that facility in Clinton  and described children living in  unsanitary conditions we spoke to one of  the lawyers Alaura mukherjee and about  what she saw many of the children had  not had access to a single shower or  bath they were wearing the same dirty  clothing that they crossed the border  with their clothes were stained with  snot with breast milk with urine and the  children didn't have access to any soap  to wash their hands there is  insufficient food for the children  nearly every child I spoke with was  hungry many of them do not have  mattresses to sleep on they don't even  have mats they're sleeping on concrete  floors Mukherjee said some of the  children had been in the facility and  Customs and Border Patrol custody for  weeks and according to federal law  unaccompanied minors must be transferred  within 72 hours that's three days to the  office of refugee resettlement which is  a special division that knows how to  deal with children now immigrant  officials have said that their  facilities are overcrowded they're  overwhelmed with more migrants come over  the southern border we actually reached  out to CBP for comment but they did not  get back to us Tony  Omar thank you very much I think one of  the questions here is why did it take  public reporting and then public outrage  before something happens like they were  shamed into it you know these children  of course deserve better and I just  think that we are better as a country  this isn't how we treat people  these are little children it's been  very very disturbing
 

